We are implementing the FINAL production version of a Java-based local agent (perfsonic-agent.jar).

This agent is the execution engine for browser automation, network capture, and real-time communication.

---

## CORE ARCHITECTURE

The agent runs locally via:
java -jar perfsonic-agent.jar

It must act as a lightweight local service.

---

1. LOCAL HTTP SERVER

---

Start HTTP server on port 4789

Expose:
GET /health → { "status": "OK", "version": "1.0.0" }

Used by frontend to detect agent availability.

---

2. WEBSOCKET CONNECTION

---

Connect to backend:
wss://<host>/auto-recorder/ws/local-agent

Responsibilities:

* Maintain persistent connection
* Send heartbeat every few seconds
* Auto-reconnect on disconnect
* Use sessionId (UUID)

---

3. COMMAND PROCESSING

---

Agent receives commands from backend via WebSocket:

Examples:

* START_SESSION
* NAVIGATE_URL
* CLICK_ELEMENT
* INPUT_TEXT
* SELECT_DROPDOWN
* SUBMIT
* CAPTURE_SNAPSHOT
* STOP_SESSION

Implement command dispatcher.

---

4. CHROME AUTOMATION (CRITICAL)

---

* Launch Chrome (headless mode)
* Connect using Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP)
* Use WebSocket debugging port

Capabilities:

* Navigate to URL
* Click elements
* Input text
* Wait for elements
* Handle page load events

---

5. SNAPSHOT STREAMING

---

* Capture screenshots using CDP
* Trigger on:

  * page navigation
  * step execution
* Send snapshot (base64) via WebSocket to backend

---

6. NETWORK CAPTURE

---

Using CDP Network domain:

Capture:

* request URL
* method
* headers
* request payload
* response body
* response status
* timing

Send structured data to backend

---

7. LOGIN HANDLING

---

* Detect login pages (DOM inspection)
* Trigger LOGIN_REQUIRED event to frontend
* Wait for credentials
* Fill username/password
* Support multi-step login
* Pause for CAPTCHA / OTP
* Resume after input

---

8. FORM HANDLING

---

* Handle:

  * text inputs
  * dropdowns
  * checkboxes
  * radio buttons

* Use stable selectors (id, name, xpath fallback)

---

9. SESSION MANAGEMENT

---

* Maintain sessionId
* Track active browser instance
* Ensure single session execution per agent

---

10. STABILITY

---

* Prevent multiple agent instances (port check)
* Handle:

  * browser crash
  * network loss
  * WebSocket reconnect
* Graceful shutdown

---

11. BUILD SETUP

---

Use Maven or Gradle to build:

perfsonic-agent.jar

---

12. CI/CD (TEKTON)

---

* Build jar in pipeline
* Copy to frontend/public/
* Include in dist

---

13. USER DISTRIBUTION

---

Provide:

* perfsonic-agent.jar
* run-agent.bat

run-agent.bat:

@echo off
start "" /min java -jar perfsonic-agent.jar

---

14. FRONTEND BEHAVIOR

---

Before recording:

Call:
http://localhost:4789/health

If NOT reachable:

Show popup:

"Agent not running.
Please start using run-agent.bat or download it below."

Provide:

* Download button
* Retry button

Do NOT detect installed vs not installed

